                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of them has you doing spaghetti loops like a Texas highway and made me want to cry. Other than that, good puzzles. Of all the games I’ve purchased solely for emoticons, this is the second I’ve comeback back to complete. \nThis one actually has a black box in the point shop and a super cute group of mini white hearts. A cat face you could use as well.\n\nYou do not need to hold the mouse button to maintain your place of where you have drawn already and honestly thank goodness \n\nYou can turn the music off, however the sound as you drag will still go off. It reminds me of a 90’s toy (plastic stick you flip) and didn’t really notice until towards the end. You may be able to turn that off too. \n\nFor completists: since I did leave this idle two hours for the emoticons, it should take you 4.5 hours or less to complete depending on your problem solving skills",
